# ==============================================================================
# SYNTHESIS CMS MINI — ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION TEMPLATE
# ==============================================================================
# This template documents the framework-neutral configuration namespaces
# used across Synthesis CMS mini.
#
# IMPORTANT SECURITY POLICY:
# - NEVER commit real credentials, secret tokens, or sensitive values.
# - Copy this template to .env or .env.local for local development.
# - All environment variables MUST be formally declared in the environment
#   contract before they can be read by runtime components.
#
# NAMESPACES & CATEGORIES:
# 1. SYNTHESIS_          : Server-only configuration (never exposed to client).
# 2. SYNTHESIS_PUBLIC_   : Client-safe public configuration (allowed in public bundles).
# 3. SYNTHESIS_SECRET_   : Sensitive server secrets (cryptographic keys, auth tokens).
# 4. SYNTHESIS_INTERNAL_ : Internal engine flags and runtime controls.
# 5. SYNTHESIS_TEST_     : Test harness and mock overrides (rejected in runtime mode).
#
# NOTE: At this baseline roadmap stage (Step 9/60), no application or database
# variables are declared. Database configuration belongs to Step 10/60.
#
# NON-CONTRACTUAL SYNTAX EXAMPLES (FOR ILLUSTRATION ONLY):
# # SYNTHESIS_PUBLIC_APP_NAME="Synthesis Mini"
# # SYNTHESIS_PORT=3000
# # SYNTHESIS_SECRET_SESSION_KEY="replace-with-secure-random-secret"
# ==============================================================================
